	(text "Links: R95 fitted (expander CS).  To drive an enable straight from J3 instead,\nfit its link (R96 ENSBC, R97 ENDAQ, R98 ENEXT), remove R95 and leave the port an input"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.5 88.9 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "04027071-79ce-4054-a2e3-f5e7b97eaf2b")
	)
	(text "C58 at VDD(SPI) pin 23, C59 at VDD(P) pin 21"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 176.53 180.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "80e36cb0-6b85-4a61-a67c-7ff474aa3bed")
	)
	(text "PCAL9714 SPI I/O expander, address 40h (ADDR = GND)\nShares CLOCK / MOSI / MISO with U1 (LTC1960); selected by nCSIO on J3.32, which was ENSBC\nPorts power up as inputs with pull-ups off: the enable pull-downs (R49, R50, R69) hold the rails off\nuntil firmware sets P0_0-P0_2 as outputs. P0_4-P0_7 read U6/U7/U9 PG and U5 nFLT. P0_3, P1_0-P1_5 spare.\nREGEN (U5 enable) stays a direct J3.12 signal and does not pass through the expander"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.5 76.2 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "e93a001c-6f43-4684-9b33-a9c2f0674d51")
	)
